  "customimageEffect": "Blend Mode",
  "customimageEffectTip": "Blend mode determines how the background texture blends with the page background color<br>Different blend modes require completely different opacity settings, adjust them together<br>1. Normal: the texture is displayed as-is without blending<br>2. Multiply: colors are multiplied, darkening the result, good for light textures<br>3. Screen: the inverse of multiply, brightening the result, good for dark textures<br>4. Overlay: darkens shadows and brightens highlights to increase contrast<br>5. Soft Light: similar to overlay but softer<br>6. Color: keeps the background brightness and applies the texture hue and saturation<br>7. Luminosity: keeps the background hue and saturation and applies the texture brightness<br>8. Color Burn: darkens the background, more noticeable with darker textures<br>9. Color Dodge: lightens the background, more noticeable with brighter textures",
